<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Skorta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Skorta was the medieval name of the mountainous district of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcadia">Arcadia</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karytaina">Karytaina</a> and the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alpheios">Alpheios</a> valley. Its Greek population was hard to control, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> of the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> held it through the barony of Karytaina. Byzantine forces recovered much of it in 1320.</p></div>
